# Local-dev secrets for the Moneta email worker.
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) and fill in real values for
# `wrangler dev`. In production, set the same names with `wrangler secret put
# <NAME>` instead — never commit real secrets, and never put them in
# wrangler.toml's [vars] since that file is plaintext and typically committed.
#
# Connecting Gmail currently uses IMAP + a Google App Password — a temporary
# stand-in for real OAuth (see worker/README.md). There's no Google Cloud
# project or API to enable for this path; the app password itself is
# supplied per-user from the Settings UI, not configured here.

# --- Firebase Admin (server-side Firestore + ID token verification) ---
# Firebase Console > Project settings > Service accounts > Generate new
# private key. Paste the entire downloaded JSON as a single-line string.
# Used to mint a Google OAuth2 access token for the Firestore REST API —
# the Worker never uses the Node firebase-admin SDK (Workers can't run it).
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=

# Must match the Firebase project the main Moneta app uses
# (VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID in the app's own .env) — used to verify that
# incoming Firebase ID tokens were issued for the right project.
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=

# --- Secret-at-rest encryption ---
# Random 32-byte key, base64-encoded, used to AES-GCM encrypt each user's
# Gmail app password before it's stored in Firestore. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
